---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead title="About — Cyan Studio" description="About the artist and the cyanotype process." />
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<div class="about-grid">
				<div class="about-text">
					<p class="page-label">About</p>
					<h1>Art made at the edge of the ocean.</h1>

					<p>
						Hi — I'm Krista, the artist behind Cyan Studio. I'm based in Ucluelet, BC,
						on the wild west coast of Vancouver Island, on the traditional territory of
						the Yuułuʔiłʔatḥ (Ucluelet) First Nation.
					</p>
					<p>
						I've been experimenting with cyanotypes for the past few years and wanted a
						space to share my prints more widely. Cyanotype is one of the oldest photographic
						processes — an image developed using ultraviolet light from the sun, producing
						that distinctive deep Prussian blue. Each composition is carefully handcrafted
						and I like to let nature do the work for me, printing hand-collected seaweeds
						and coastal botanicals from right here in Ucluelet.
					</p>
					<p>
						When I'm not making art, I study seaweed for a living — working on kelp and
						nearshore habitat mapping, monitoring, and restoration. The ocean is both my
						workplace and my studio.
					</p>
					<p>
						Each print is carefully created using archival quality paper and packaging
						materials, so your piece will last.
					</p>

					<div class="about-divider"></div>

					<h2>The process</h2>
					<div class="process-list">
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">01</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Gather</strong>
								<p>Seaweeds and coastal botanicals are collected by hand from the shoreline around Ucluelet — kelp, rockweed, sea lettuce, feather boa kelp, and whatever the tide brings in.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">02</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Coat</strong>
								<p>Archival watercolour paper is coated with a light-sensitive cyanotype solution — a mix of ferric ammonium citrate and potassium ferricyanide — and left to dry in the dark.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">03</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Compose &amp; expose</strong>
								<p>The botanicals are arranged on the coated paper and placed in direct sunlight. UV light does the work — exposure time varies with the season and cloud cover.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
						<div class="process-item">
							<span class="p-num">04</span>
							<div>
								<strong>Develop</strong>
								<p>The paper is rinsed in water. Where light hit, the characteristic Prussian blue develops. Where the botanicals blocked the light, the paper stays white — a perfect silhouette.</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

				<aside class="about-aside">
					<div class="aside-card">
						<h3>Originals</h3>
						<p>Each original is a unique, one-of-a-kind piece — no two are ever the same. Signed and titled on the reverse.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="aside-card">
						<h3>Prints</h3>
						<p>Limited edition reproductions on archival paper. A more accessible way to bring a piece of the coast into your home.</p>
					</div>
					<div class="aside-card">
						<h3>Materials</h3>
						<p>All prints are made on acid-free, archival quality paper. Packaging is plastic-free and fully recyclable.</p>
					</div>
					<a href="/contact" class="aside-cta">Get in touch →</a>
				</aside>
			</div>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>

<style>
	main {
		max-width: 960px;
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 3em 1.5em 5em;
	}
	.page-label {
		font-size: 0.72em;
		letter-spacing: 0.18em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--cyan-mid);
		margin: 0 0 0.75em;
	}
	h1 {
		font-size: 2.4em;
		color: var(--prussian);
		line-height: 1.15;
		margin: 0 0 1.25em;
		max-width: 18ch;
	}
	h2 {
		font-size: 1.25em;
		color: var(--prussian);
		margin: 0 0 1.25em;
	}
	p {
		color: var(--text-muted);
		line-height: 1.8;
		margin: 0 0 1.1em;
		font-size: 0.95em;
	}
	.about-grid {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 1fr 300px;
		gap: 4em;
		align-items: start;
	}
	.about-divider {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
		margin: 2em 0;
	}
	.process-list {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1.5em;
	}
	.process-item {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1.25em;
	}
	.p-num {
		font-size: 0.7em;
		letter-spacing: 0.1em;
		color: var(--cyan-mid);
		padding-top: 0.3em;
		flex-shrink: 0;
		width: 1.5em;
	}
	.process-item strong {
		display: block;
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--prussian);
		margin-bottom: 0.3em;
	}
	.process-item p {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.88em;
	}

	/* ── Aside ── */
	.about-aside {
		display: flex;
		flex-direction: column;
		gap: 1em;
		position: sticky;
		top: 2em;
	}
	.aside-card {
		background: var(--cyan-pale);
		border-radius: 8px;
		padding: 1.25em 1.5em;
		border: 1px solid var(--border);
	}
	.aside-card h3 {
		font-size: 0.85em;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--prussian);
		margin: 0 0 0.5em;
	}
	.aside-card p {
		font-size: 0.82em;
		margin: 0;
	}
	.aside-cta {
		display: block;
		text-align: center;
		background: var(--prussian);
		color: var(--sand-light);
		padding: 0.85em;
		border-radius: 6px;
		text-decoration: none;
		font-size: 0.85em;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		margin-top: 0.5em;
		transition: background 0.2s;
	}
	.aside-cta:hover { background: var(--prussian-dark); color: var(--sand-light); }

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.about-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 2em; }
		.about-aside { position: static; }
		h1 { font-size: 1.9em; }
	}
</style>
